{title: 545 - Savior, Like a Shepherd}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #545 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 545}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Db]Savior, like a shepherd lead us,
[Ab]Much we [Db/Ab]need [Ab7]Thy tenderest [Db]care;
[Db]In Thy pleasant pastures [Ab7]feed us,
[Db]For our use [Gb]Thy folds prepare.
[Db]Blessed Jesus, blessed Jesus!
[Ab]Thou [Ab7]hast bought us, [Db]Thine we are.
[Gb]Blessed Jesus, [Db]blessed Jesus!
[Db]Thou hast bought [Ab7]us, Thine we [Db]are.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Db]We are thine, thou dost befriend us,
[Ab]be [Db/Ab]the [Ab7]guardian of our [Db]way;
[Db]keep thy flock, from sin [Ab]defend [Ab7]us,
[Db]seek us when [Gb]we go astray.
[Db]Blessed Jesus, blessed Jesus!
[Ab]Hear, [Ab7]O hear us [Db]when we pray.
[Gb]Blessed Jesus, [Db]blessed Jesus!
[Db]Hear, O hear [Ab7]us when we [Db]pray.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Db]Thou hast promised to receive us,
[Ab]poor [Db/Ab]and [Ab7]sinful though we [Db]be;
[Db]thou hast mercy to [Ab]relieve [Ab7]us,
[Db]grace to cleanse and [Gb]power to free.
[Db]Blessed Jesus, blessed Jesus!
[Ab]We [Ab7]will early [Db]turn to thee.
[Gb]Blessed Jesus, [Db]blessed Jesus!
[Db]We will early [Ab7]turn to [Db]thee.
{end_of_verse}
